menu "Denon/Spotify Controller"

config DSC_FACTORY_TEST
    bool "Build factory test mode instead of the application"
    default n
    help
        Manufacturing hardware exerciser (docs/SECURITY.md §7b). Must never
        be enabled in a shipping build -- tools/check_release.py fails a
        production profile that has this set.

config DSC_PROV_AP_SSID_PREFIX
    string "Provisioning SoftAP SSID prefix"
    default "DSC-Setup"
    help
        net_wifi appends a MAC-derived suffix (docs/SECURITY.md §5). Read by
        app_wiring, injected into net_wifi_cfg_t -- net_wifi.c itself never
        references a CONFIG_ symbol directly.

config DSC_SNTP_SERVER
    string "SNTP server"
    default "pool.ntp.org"
    help
        Read by app_wiring, injected into net_time_cfg_t.

config DSC_OTA_MANIFEST_URL
    string "OTA manifest URL"
    default "https://ota.example.com/manifest.json"
    help
        Read by app_wiring, injected into svc_ota_cfg_t. docs/PLATFORM.md §2.3.

config DSC_OTA_FORCE_CHECK_ON_BOOT
    bool "Check for OTA update immediately on boot (dev convenience)"
    default n
    help
        Skips the randomised daily-check wait for the first check this
        boot. Never set in a production profile.

config DSC_TEST_FORCE_HEALTH_GATE_TIMEOUT
    bool "Force the post-OTA health gate to time out (test only)"
    default n
    help
        Suppresses the HEALTH_COND_BOOT_COMPLETE report so the health gate
        can never reach PASS, only TIMED_OUT after its window -- exists
        solely to exercise the automatic-rollback path on real hardware
        (docs/ROADMAP.md Tier 7's rollback proof). Must never be enabled
        in a shipping build -- tools/check_release.py fails a production
        profile that has this set.

config DSC_DENON_DEBUG_CONSOLE
    bool "Start a UART debug console for exercising svc_denon (dev convenience)"
    default n
    help
        docs/ROADMAP.md Phase 3's "crude debug UI" bullet, implemented as
        an esp_console REPL over UART instead of on-screen text -- no
        hal_display/LVGL bring-up exists yet (Phase 5 scope). Commands:
        denon status|host|power|volume|mute|input|mode|fuzz. Not a
        production feature -- tools/check_release.py fails a production
        profile that has this set, same as DSC_FACTORY_TEST.

config DSC_DENON_SELFTEST
    bool "Run a scripted svc_denon self-test after boot (test only)"
    default n
    help
        Once the link reaches CONNECTED_TELNET/CONNECTED_HTTP, submits a
        scripted sequence of real intents (power/input/volume/mute/mode,
        including a request above volume_limit_max to prove the safety
        clamp holds) through the real intent queue, then a fuzzed burst of
        volume intents -- docs/ROADMAP.md Phase 3's exit criterion, on real
        hardware. Exists because scripting interactive console input over
        this board's native USB-CDC port proved unreliable from Windows;
        this needs only read-only UART capture to verify. Must never be
        enabled in a shipping build -- tools/check_release.py fails a
        production profile that has this set, same as DSC_FACTORY_TEST.

config DSC_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID
    string "Spotify app client_id (dev convenience default)"
    default ""
    help
        Not confidential under PKCE (no client_secret involved), unlike
        wifi.psk, which never gets a Kconfig-baked default. Read once by
        app_wiring and used to seed the secure NVS namespace ONLY if
        nothing is already stored there -- `spotify client-id <id>`
        overrides at runtime regardless of this default.

config DSC_SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URI
    string "Spotify app redirect_uri (dev convenience default)"
    default ""
    help
        A loopback address (http://127.0.0.1:<port>/callback) per this
        project's Phase 4 plan -- registering an arbitrary HTTPS domain
        risks a real third party seeing the OAuth code in transit; a
        loopback address never leaves the user's own machine even as an
        attempted connection. Same seed-only-if-empty treatment as
        DSC_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID; `spotify redirect-uri <uri>` overrides at
        runtime.

config DSC_SPOTIFY_DEBUG_CONSOLE
    bool "Register the `spotify` UART debug console command family (dev convenience)"
    default n
    help
        Same esp_console REPL Phase 3's DSC_DENON_DEBUG_CONSOLE started --
        this flag independently gates registering the `spotify` command
        set (pair|code|unpair|client-id|redirect-uri|devices|
        set-avr-device|clear-avr-device|status|play|pause|next|prev|
        shuffle|repeat|volume) alongside it. Not a production feature --
        tools/check_release.py fails a production profile that has this
        set, same as DSC_DENON_DEBUG_CONSOLE.

config DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR
    bool "Run scripted Spotify pairing after boot using Kconfig-seeded values (test only)"
    default n
    help
        Same reasoning as DSC_DENON_SELFTEST: scripting interactive console
        input over this board's native USB-CDC port proved unreliable from
        Windows. When enabled, and no refresh token is already stored, the
        device automatically begins pairing at boot (equivalent to `spotify
        pair`) and logs the authorize URL -- read-only over UART, no typing
        needed. If DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR_CODE is also set, its value is
        submitted automatically (equivalent to `spotify code <url>`), so a
        second flash with that value filled in completes pairing with zero
        live console interaction. Must never be enabled in a shipping
        build -- tools/check_release.py fails a production profile that has
        this set, same as DSC_DENON_SELFTEST.

config DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR_CODE
    string "Pasted OAuth callback URL for DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR (test only)"
    default ""
    depends on DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR
    help
        The full address-bar URL copied after approving access on Spotify's
        consent screen (contains ?code=...&state=...). Left empty on the
        first flash (which only prints the authorize URL); filled in and
        reflashed once you have it.

config DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR_VERIFIER
    string "Fixed PKCE code_verifier for DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR (test only)"
    default "9z0VM7MCOfJi5yCMfSlEq6xrgrj3T3zwo2diJK0eSfo"
    depends on DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR
    help
        svc_spotify_begin_pair() normally generates a fresh, random PKCE
        verifier/state on every call -- fine for the interactive `spotify
        pair` console command, which stays running between generating the
        URL and receiving the code, but DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR's whole reason
        for existing is that live console interaction over this board's
        native USB-CDC port is unreliable, forcing a two-boot flow (print
        URL, reflash with the code). A fresh random verifier/state on the
        second boot would never match what the first boot's URL was built
        from. Fixing the verifier/state as source-level constants instead
        means both boots derive the identical code_challenge/state, with no
        dependency on anything (NVS, a live write) surviving the reflash in
        between. The default here is a real, validly-formatted (43-char
        base64url, RFC 7636 §4.1) example value, not a placeholder -- safe
        to use as-is since it only ever pairs with this device's own
        client_id/redirect_uri, both already under your control.

config DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR_STATE
    string "Fixed OAuth state nonce for DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR (test only)"
    default "1ac76f466aa55c6949a2f18afd13f8b5"
    depends on DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR
    help
        Pairs with DSC_SPOTIFY_AUTOPAIR_VERIFIER above -- same reasoning,
        same fixed-across-both-boots requirement. A real, validly-formatted
        (32 hex chars, matching spotify_auth.c's own random_hex(..., 16))
        example value, not a placeholder.

endmenu
